/-!
# Checked rank-one certificate for the literal HS twenty-space

The four words and descending polynomial in `../source/density.json` give
an element P of the algebra generated by the original matrices A and B.
Horner evaluation is checked one multiplication/addition at a time. The
certificate also checks P = u r, r u = 1, the twenty left and right word
translates of P, and the two orbit-basis inverse identities.

All arithmetic is kernel-checked with the proved packed binary row checker.
The JSON and this file's generator supply witnesses only. Matrices retain
the original ATLAS rows; neither transpose nor inverse changes the action.

Source: R. A. Wilson et al., ATLAS HSG1-f2r20B0, and the deterministic
certificate discovery in `Twenty/source/discover_density.py`.
Generated by `Absolute/source/generate.py`.
-/

